[{"id": 102771, "post_id": 1113142, "parent": 0, "user": "Aszaunmi", "user_id": 38034, "date": "2026-09-29 03:24:09", "date_gmt": "2026-09-29 01:24:09", "date_gmt_iso": "2026-09-29T01:24:09+00:00", "content": "The shaft of my motor appears to be shorter than shown in the photo.  Everything lines up but the photo does not match what I see once my new pulley.", "type": "comment", "role": "visitor", "replies": []}, {"id": 102512, "post_id": 1113142, "parent": 0, "user": "Pyros777", "user_id": 180767, "date": "2026-09-25 21:50:45", "date_gmt": "2026-09-25 19:50:45", "date_gmt_iso": "2026-09-25T19:50:45+00:00", "content": "The shaft on my original Core One (non-plus) motor is also shorter than pictured, fyi.", "type": "comment", "role": "visitor", "replies": [{"id": 102733, "post_id": 1113142, "parent": 102512, "user": "George", "user_id": 29382, "date": "2026-09-28 17:07:30", "date_gmt": "2026-09-28 15:07:30", "date_gmt_iso": "2026-09-28T15:07:30+00:00", "content": "Same. as long as the pulleys are at the right offset from the motor itself it shouldn&#039;t matter. I guess i&#039;ll find out at the end of the whole thing :D", "type": "comment", "role": "visitor", "replies": []}]}, {"id": 101851, "post_id": 1113142, "parent": 0, "user": "iKriz", "user_id": 168027, "date": "2026-09-18 21:35:46", "date_gmt": "2026-09-18 19:35:46", "date_gmt_iso": "2026-09-18T19:35:46+00:00", "content": "the shaft looks longer than mine...........", "type": "comment", "role": "visitor", "replies": [{"id": 102482, "post_id": 1113142, "parent": 101851, "user": "Philcotigo", "user_id": 108526, "date": "2026-09-25 11:06:14", "date_gmt": "2026-09-25 09:06:14", "date_gmt_iso": "2026-09-25T09:06:14+00:00", "content": "I measured 20.4mm stick out from the black face. (coming from the 2025 MK4s &gt; C1 upgrade)\nWith that and the Y-side of the offset tool the shaft is 1.6mm too short.", "type": "comment", "role": "visitor", "replies": []}]}, {"id": 101733, "post_id": 1113142, "parent": 0, "user": "TerryM", "user_id": 15990, "date": "2026-09-17 12:42:13", "date_gmt": "2026-09-17 10:42:13", "date_gmt_iso": "2026-09-17T10:42:13+00:00", "content": "Same. Even with the screws out and lube in I had to almost hit them in. There is no flat side in the pulleys. I think they have messed up", "type": "comment", "role": "visitor", "replies": [{"id": 102483, "post_id": 1113142, "parent": 101733, "user": "Philcotigo", "user_id": 108526, "date": "2026-09-25 11:07:48", "date_gmt": "2026-09-25 09:07:48", "date_gmt_iso": "2026-09-25T09:07:48+00:00", "content": "the flat is for the screw to securely grab (grub) onto the motor shaft. it is not designed to have the flat shaped into the inside of the pulley. so you&#039;re good.", "type": "comment", "role": "visitor", "replies": []}]}, {"id": 100600, "post_id": 1113142, "parent": 0, "user": "Ben Dover", "user_id": 46415, "date": "2026-09-05 17:37:59", "date_gmt": "2026-09-05 15:37:59", "date_gmt_iso": "2026-09-05T15:37:59+00:00", "content": "For some reason my pulley was a very tight fit (even when grub screws were loosened).  Took a good bit of force to get them on there.", "type": "comment", "role": "visitor", "replies": [{"id": 100892, "post_id": 1113142, "parent": 100600, "user": "anelson", "user_id": 90588, "date": "2026-09-07 21:20:26", "date_gmt": "2026-09-07 19:20:26", "date_gmt_iso": "2026-09-07T19:20:26+00:00", "content": "I had the same problem, caused by burrs in the motor shaft from tightening the grub screw. A small precision file will knock those down and make it slide on easily.", "type": "comment", "role": "visitor", "replies": []}]}, {"id": 100405, "post_id": 1113142, "parent": 0, "user": "Nicholas Borge", "user_id": 170278, "date": "2026-09-03 20:13:47", "date_gmt": "2026-09-03 18:13:47", "date_gmt_iso": "2026-09-03T18:13:47+00:00", "content": "There are two set screws on each pulley. which of the two are we to be tightening &quot;against the flat of the motor shaft&quot;?", "type": "comment", "role": "visitor", "replies": [{"id": 100406, "post_id": 1113142, "parent": 100405, "user": "Nicholas Borge", "user_id": 170278, "date": "2026-09-03 20:15:20", "date_gmt": "2026-09-03 18:15:20", "date_gmt_iso": "2026-09-03T18:15:20+00:00", "content": "I now see it&#039;s the lower of the two in the later image...", "type": "comment", "role": "visitor", "replies": [{"id": 102478, "post_id": 1113142, "parent": 100406, "user": "Vojta Zeman", "user_id": 83180, "date": "2026-09-25 10:02:23", "date_gmt": "2026-09-25 08:02:23", "date_gmt_iso": "2026-09-25T08:02:23+00:00", "content": "Hello. It doesn&#039;t matter which one.", "type": "comment", "role": "employee", "replies": []}]}]}, {"id": 99614, "post_id": 1113142, "parent": 0, "user": "wubbr", "user_id": 160344, "date": "2026-08-24 12:13:41", "date_gmt": "2026-08-24 10:13:41", "date_gmt_iso": "2026-08-24T10:13:41+00:00", "content": "The shaft on my motor seems shorter", "type": "comment", "role": "visitor", "replies": [{"id": 99982, "post_id": 1113142, "parent": 99614, "user": "Clumsy-Creator", "user_id": 212014, "date": "2026-08-30 15:34:19", "date_gmt": "2026-08-30 13:34:19", "date_gmt_iso": "2026-08-30T13:34:19+00:00", "content": "Yeah mine but only 3mm, so it won&#039;t make diference. Mines a core one plus originally.", "type": "comment", "role": "visitor", "replies": []}, {"id": 100172, "post_id": 1113142, "parent": 99614, "user": "eliotik", "user_id": 107190, "date": "2026-08-31 22:39:24", "date_gmt": "2026-08-31 20:39:24", "date_gmt_iso": "2026-08-31T20:39:24+00:00", "content": "same here, about 3mm shorter shaft, original core one.", "type": "comment", "role": "visitor", "replies": []}, {"id": 102426, "post_id": 1113142, "parent": 99614, "user": "Stephen", "user_id": 183927, "date": "2026-09-24 21:11:53", "date_gmt": "2026-09-24 19:11:53", "date_gmt_iso": "2026-09-24T19:11:53+00:00", "content": "Same, not a good 3mm or so, doubt that matters.", "type": "comment", "role": "visitor", "replies": []}]}, {"id": 99579, "post_id": 1113142, "parent": 0, "user": "Käsekuchen", "user_id": 47677, "date": "2026-08-23 16:30:30", "date_gmt": "2026-08-23 14:30:30", "date_gmt_iso": "2026-08-23T14:30:30+00:00", "content": "The shaft end doesn&#039;t line up with the pulley on my end. Like on the picture", "type": "comment", "role": "visitor", "replies": [{"id": 99619, "post_id": 1113142, "parent": 99579, "user": "anden3", "user_id": 193074, "date": "2026-08-24 16:46:59", "date_gmt": "2026-08-24 14:46:59", "date_gmt_iso": "2026-08-24T14:46:59+00:00", "content": "Same here.", "type": "comment", "role": "visitor", "replies": [{"id": 99862, "post_id": 1113142, "parent": 99619, "user": "WorstCase", "user_id": 21359, "date": "2026-08-29 10:24:37", "date_gmt": "2026-08-29 08:24:37", "date_gmt_iso": "2026-08-29T08:24:37+00:00", "content": "Same here too. Maybe because I originally had a Core One (without Plus)", "type": "comment", "role": "visitor", "replies": [{"id": 100971, "post_id": 1113142, "parent": 99862, "user": "Steve Stratoti", "user_id": 209860, "date": "2026-09-08 17:32:42", "date_gmt": "2026-09-08 15:32:42", "date_gmt_iso": "2026-09-08T15:32:42+00:00", "content": "I have a plus and its the same, the shaft is depressed inside the pulley but a few mm", "type": "comment", "role": "visitor", "replies": []}]}]}]}, {"id": 99342, "post_id": 1113142, "parent": 0, "user": "k1mu", "user_id": 94890, "date": "2026-08-16 21:17:55", "date_gmt": "2026-08-16 19:17:55", "date_gmt_iso": "2026-08-16T19:17:55+00:00", "content": "It&#039;s important to make sure the part of the pulley with the grub screws is near the motor.", "type": "comment", "role": "visitor", "replies": [{"id": 99391, "post_id": 1113142, "parent": 99342, "user": "Vojta Zeman", "user_id": 83180, "date": "2026-08-18 07:37:02", "date_gmt": "2026-08-18 05:37:02", "date_gmt_iso": "2026-08-18T05:37:02+00:00", "content": "Good catch! We’ve added this important detail to the instructions.", "type": "comment", "role": "employee", "replies": []}, {"id": 102487, "post_id": 1113142, "parent": 99342, "user": "Dries De Smet", "user_id": 168263, "date": "2026-09-25 11:48:31", "date_gmt": "2026-09-25 09:48:31", "date_gmt_iso": "2026-09-25T09:48:31+00:00", "content": "heh. thanks! was looking through the gantry thinking &quot;this doesn&#039;t look right&quot; so went back through comments and this made me go &quot;aaaaah&quot;", "type": "comment", "role": "visitor", "replies": []}]}]